comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-05T18:10:28.694Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check before filing (2026-08-05): searched the full corpus for recursive self improvement, self-improvement loops, and 'pm improves itself using its own tracker data'. The hits are all narrower and all real neighbours rather than duplicates — pm-cc04 is an ADR for agent self-repair through a remediation registry, pm-dhrp was a validation auto-fix session, pm-0682l4 and pm-k9t17l are self-reference guards in install and ordering. Nothing composes the measurement surfaces into a cycle.\n\nWhat exists is substrate, not a loop: pm-ips23h ratchets filed populations so they cannot grow, pm-1qkivy turns resolved incident patterns into gates, pm-rtn5h6 requires every escaped defect to land the gate that would have caught it, pm-pww8ax ratchets dogfood coverage, pm-qd6gvf projects the record as trajectories, pm-8pnj measures tokens per completed task, pm-2vs1za compares measured cost against forecast value. Each answers one question about one pass. None answers 'is pm getting better, by how much, measured how' across passes.\n\nThe asymmetry that motivates the ledger child: a ceiling can only ever prove a number did not grow. Every measurement the project ratchets is therefore blind to improvement — the one direction the loop needs to observe."
body: ""
